For twenty years, getting found online meant ranking on Google. That still matters. But more and more buyers now skip the search results and ask an AI assistant directly: "Which agency builds good Shopify stores in Pune?" or "Best skincare brand for oily skin?"

The assistant gives one answer, often with a few names. Answer Engine Optimisation (AEO) is the work of making sure your business is one of them.

## How AI assistants decide who to recommend

Assistants build answers from content they can find, understand and trust. Three things help them pick you:

- Clear answers on your own site. Pages that say plainly what you do, who it's for, where you work and what it costs.
- Structure machines can read. Headings, FAQs and schema markup that spell out your services, prices and locations.
- Proof from other places. Reviews, directory listings and mentions on sites the assistant already trusts.

## AEO vs SEO: do you need both?

Yes, and they overlap a lot. Good SEO (fast pages, clear headings, useful content) is the foundation AEO is built on. AEO adds a focus on direct answers, FAQs and being cited, not just clicked.

## Five things you can do this month

- Add an FAQ section to every service page, answering the questions customers actually ask you.
- Put prices, or at least "starting from" prices, on your site. Assistants love concrete numbers.
- Make sure your Google Business Profile is complete and your reviews are recent.
- Write one honest comparison page, for example "Website vs app: what does my business need?"
- Ask ChatGPT and Gemini about your category and note who they mention. That's your competition now.

> If an assistant can't explain what you do in one sentence, it won't recommend you.

